<% if (SHOW_TESTIMONIALS) { %>
<!-- Testimonials: do not attribute quotes to invented people. Real quotes
     and names, once collected from an actual parent, school contact, and
     caterer partner, replace the bracketed text below — flip
     SHOW_TESTIMONIALS at the top of this file to bring it back. -->
<section class="section on-tint" id="testimonials">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">What people say</span>
      <h2>In their own words — once we have them.</h2>
      <p>Real quotes from a parent, a school, and a caterer partner will go here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="testimonial-card testimonial-pending" data-reveal data-reveal-group="testimonials">
        <span class="testimonial-role">Parent</span>
        <p>"[Quote pending — real testimonial from a parent using Evo Meals]"</p>
        <span class="testimonial-name">[Name], parent</span>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-card testimonial-pending" data-reveal data-reveal-group="testimonials">
        <span class="testimonial-role">School</span>
        <p>"[Quote pending — real testimonial from a partner school]"</p>
        <span class="testimonial-name">[Name], [Title] at [School]</span>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-card testimonial-pending" data-reveal data-reveal-group="testimonials">
        <span class="testimonial-role">Caterer</span>
        <p>"[Quote pending — real testimonial from a catering partner]"</p>
        <span class="testimonial-name">[Name], [Kitchen/Company]</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<% } %>

<section class="proof-section">
  <div class="wrap-wide proof-wrap">
    <div class="proof-intro" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Where Evo Meals is used</span>
      <p>Not a pilot, not a pitch deck — live at real schools today, booked by real parents, tapped in by real students every school day.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="proof-names">
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">American Creativity Academy</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">Kuwait English School</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">The English School</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-tint" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions people actually ask</span>
      <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
      <p>Grouped by topic so you can jump straight to yours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-groups">
      <div class="faq-group" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-group-head">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"/></svg>
          <h3>Booking</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item is-open">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="true"><span>How does the "tap" actually work?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Your child carries a school-issued meal card. At the counter, they tap it against the reader — that single tap confirms their booking, marks the meal collected, and updates your dashboard within moments. No PIN and no cash changes hands.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-group-head">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M2 10h20"/></svg>
          <h3>Payments</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Is my payment information safe?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Payments go through KNET, Kuwait's national payment gateway — Evo Meals never stores your card details. Your child's Civil ID is masked everywhere it's shown in the app, including to you.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-group-head">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3 4 6v6c0 4.4 3.4 8.4 8 9 4.6-.6 8-4.6 8-9V6l-8-3Z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
          <h3>Allergies &amp; Safety</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>My child has an allergy. How does that get handled?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You list allergies on their student profile once, and it's shown to the catering and serving staff preparing your child's meals. Dishes carry their own allergen information — nut-free, shellfish-free, sesame-free, soy-free, and more, where applicable — but this is per-dish information, not an independently verified guarantee, so check the dish's own detail if your child has a specific allergy.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-group-head">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="m9 9 6 6m0-6-6 6"/></svg>
          <h3>Cancellations</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>What if I need to cancel a booking?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Cancel any upcoming booking from your history page before the meal is collected. The full amount is refunded straight back to your original payment method — no ticket, no waiting on a refund process.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" data-reveal>
        <div class="faq-group-head">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 21V9l8-5 8 5v12"/><path d="M9 21v-6h6v6"/></svg>
          <h3>Schools &amp; Caterers</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How does a school actually bring Evo Meals in?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Get in touch through the <a href="/schools">For Schools</a> page or the contact form. We set up your menu, plans, and parent onboarding together before your program goes live — there's no self-serve signup for schools.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How does a caterer get set up on the platform?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Caterers connect through the <a href="/caterers">For Caterers</a> page. We match you to a school's program and get your kitchen onto the digital order queue before day one.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Can school staff use Evo Meals too?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes — staff have their own meal booking flow, separate from student accounts, at a fixed staff meal price.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="wrap-wide cta-inner">
    <div class="cta-copy" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Ready when you are</span>
      <h2>Ready to transform your school's meal program?</h2>
      <p>Partner with Evo Meals — set up a program, a kitchen, or a family account in about two minutes.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/schools" class="btn btn-primary">Partner With Us</a>
        <a href="/register" class="btn btn-ghost">Create an Account</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-echo" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="cta-echo-label">This is what parents see</span>
      <div class="cta-echo-toast">
        <span class="cta-echo-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span>
        <div>
          <div class="cta-echo-title">Ahmed tapped in — lunch collected</div>
          <div class="cta-echo-sub">12:14 PM · Arabiatta Chicken Pasta</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/sitefoot') %>

</body>
</html>
